{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-frobenius-self-duality-forces-lp-dual-extraction","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:frobenius-self-duality-forces-lp-dual-extraction","kind":"proposition","title":"Frobenius self-duality of $(H_n(R,q),\\tau)$ forces $\\tau$-extraction to produce LP-dual variables","tags":["frobenius-self-duality","lp-duality","shadow-price","markov-trace","observation-frame","structural-justification"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction","text":"frobenius-self-duality-forces-lp-dual-extraction.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:frobenius-self-duality-forces-lp-dual-extraction\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I_n \\subset H_n(R,q)</code> be the radical of the Markov trace\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau</code>, the sum of the Wedderburn blocks <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_\\lambda</code> with\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">y_\\lambda = 0</code>. At the Markov parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z = q^3/(q^2+1)</code> these are the shapes with three\nor more rows, so <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I_n = 0</code> for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n \\le 2</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_n/I_n = TL_n(q)</code>.\nThe trace descends to a non-degenerate symmetric bilinear pairing\non <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">TL_n(q)</code>. This makes <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(TL_n(q),\\tau)</code> a Frobenius algebra,\nhence canonically isomorphic to its <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-linear dual. Under this isomorphism, the primal LP variable\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">x \\in TL_n</code> and the dual LP variable <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u \\in TL_n^*</code> live in the\nsame space, and the Observation Frame\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Obs}_\\tau(a) := \\tau(a \\cdot -)</code> extracts the\nshadow-price representative of every observable.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-self-duality-forces-lp-dual-extraction.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.21.21","page":"b/prop-frobenius-self-duality-forces-lp-dual-extraction","qa":{"counts":{"pass":61,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":53,"unknown":0,"stale":104},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FrobeniusSelfDualityForcesLPDualExtraction.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
